      "agent": "opencode:postbox",
      "impact_assessment": {
        "why": "A verified probe shows chunked POSTs are rejected with 400, so a sender using Transfer-Encoding: chunked cannot be captured at all.",
        "benefits": "Postbox captures bodies from standard HTTP clients that stream without Content-Length.",
        "risks": "contract: chunked changes from 400 to accepted, so README and ADR must follow; dependency: stdlib only; concurrency: the decoder runs before the store lock and cannot block it; state: a malformed stream must never produce a partial record.",
        "mitigation": "Bound every readline, cap the accumulated body at max_body, return 400/413 before constructing a record, and use raw-socket known-answer tests."
